      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Just nine miles east of Bismarck, Apple Valley sits on the north side of Apple Creek’s valley, a tributary of the Missouri River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Valley%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Perched at about 1,680 feet, Apple Valley enjoys a humid continental climate with cold winters, warm humid summers, and a 52‑inch snowfall average.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        19,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/apple_valley_north_dakota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Apple Valley’s flood risk is rated severe, reflecting its low‑lying position near Apple Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
